# BACKLOG.md uses hand-maintained Markdown tables with wide status emoji
# (✅ 🔄 ⬜ ❌ ⏭️). Prettier measures those emoji as 1 column while editors
# render them as 2, so its auto-padding misaligns every status row. Keep it
# out of Prettier so the compact, drift-free table format stays put.
BACKLOG.md

# docs/qa-recheck.md is the same class of file, one level down: a hand-worked
# checklist whose state lives INSIDE the checkbox — `[ ]` → `[🔁]` → `[✅]` /
# `[❌ …]`. Only `[ ]` and `[x]` are GFM task-list markers, so the moment a row
# carries a status emoji Prettier stops seeing a task item and re-indents its
# continuation lines from 6 columns to 2. Marking 51 rows rewrote 184, and every
# tester pass would churn the file again. It is generated by
# `node scripts/qa-recheck.js`, which owns the layout; keep Prettier out of it.
docs/qa-recheck.md

# The OpenAPI contract is machine-written by `npm run swagger:export -w
# apps/store-api` as `JSON.stringify(document, null, 2)` — no trailing newline.
# lint-staged's `*.json` rule would reformat it on every commit, after which the
# committed file could never again equal a fresh export, and the
# `contract-freshness` CI job (which compares them byte-for-byte) would be red
# forever. Never format this file by hand or by tool; regenerate it.
apps/store-api/swagger.json
